      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily** with meals, a common regimen\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
